<title>JAPAN: Japan Feb rubber imports fall 8.9 pct yr/yr--MOF.</title>
<headline>Japan Feb rubber imports fall 8.9 pct yr/yr--MOF.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's rubber imports in February totalled 62,135 tonnes, down 8.9 percent from a year earlier, Finance Ministry data released on Friday showed.</p>
<p>Figures were as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>			Feb 97	 Jan 97	Feb 96</p>
<p> Total		62,135	 63,921	68,206</p>
<p>Major suppliers:</p>
<p> Thailand	   48,990	 44,668	52,975</p>
<p> Indonesia	   7,270	 13,819	10,029</p>
<p> Malaysia	    4,577	  4,025	 3,852</p>
<p>Total imports in the first two months of calendar 1997 were 126,056 tonnes against 129,491 in the same period a year earlier.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk (+81-3-3432-7391)</p>
</text>
